xnu: 0087 sweet startall daif drill

drill: 0087 sweet startall daif drill

The 0086 marker beats print on the first processor_start but the
second call still dies between the "P0084 ... reason=1" beat and the
0086 pre beat, i.e. before the in-function mask was armed. Move the
exception mask to the caller: SweetCPU::startAll masks IRQ/FIQ/
SError/Debug right before the processor_start() call and unmasks after
(if it ever returns). Evidence matrix:
- "DAIF masked, entering" prints but the deeper nails still stop at
  reason=1   -> the second call dies fully masked: not an async
               exception; suspect the kprintf/console path next
- deeper nails (P0086 pre) now print -> async exception confirmed,
  because the mask was the thing that changed the outcome
- boot passes the call entirely -> solved, unmask and walk on

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
@@ -168,4 +168,16 @@ SweetCPU::startAll(void *arg __unused, wait_result_t result __unused)
 		kprintf("P0084: startAll: cpu=%u before processor_start\n", i);
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+		/* 0087: the 0086 mask inside processor.c was armed micro-
+		 * seconds before the death and never printed on the second
+		 * call. Block every exception already at the caller and
+		 * unmask only when the call itself returns. */
+		__asm__ volatile("msr daifset, #0xf; dmb ish; isb" ::: "memory");
+		kprintf("P0087: startAll: cpu=%u DAIF masked, entering processor_start\n", i);
+#endif
 		kern_return_t kr = processor_start(cpu->machProcessor);
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+		kprintf("P0087: startAll: cpu=%u processor_start returned kr=%d\n", i, (int)kr);
+		__asm__ volatile("msr daifclr, #0xf; dmb ish" ::: "memory");
+#endif
 		kprintf("P0084: startAll: cpu=%u processor_start returned %d\n", i, kr);
 		if (kr != KERN_SUCCESS) {

